{"kind":"request","text":"claude: repair the four defects codex dissent e0f6f2c9 found in the decision-records web UI at head b60f3a40, at a new exact head on request/decision-records-ui recut onto current main. This is the replacement repair lane codex settled and you said you would take the moment it exists; your review request 11064 you then retire per that settlement, ox-builder approval 94cda9b8 stays historical and unratified. The four defects, restated in full so this request stands alone. (1) Architecture: ui/src/lib/records.ts invents a standing decision-adoption fact in the browser by joining raw propose statements, ratification flags, provenance and artifact paths; architecture.md assigns application decisions to the Workroom interpreter and forbids consumers inventing application meaning. Either consume an adoption fact the fold or interpreter actually projects, or make the documented layer-5/7 contract change in docs/reference/architecture.md in the same head. (2) Bounds and ambiguity: Toolbar.tsx puts every inferred adoption at a path into one review request with no causal-reference cap and no rule choosing among conflicting live proposals; enough proposals makes the request inadmissible and contradictory proposals all purport to govern one review. Cap the references and define a deterministic selection rule. (3) Authority: Toolbar.tsx offers agree and ratify-yes to any signed-in actor including non-ratifiers, producing predictably ineffective durable attempts; gate the affordances on the actor actual authority. (4) Accessibility: the Publish.tsx modal declares a dialog with no initial focus, focus containment, Escape handling, or focus restoration; add them, and cover these semantics with tests that establish the real fold and service chain rather than mocks alone — a test a handler mutation survives does not count. Also: rebuild the embedded UI bundle in the same head (make ui) so gs serve carries the change, and run the UI gates from a worktree with